WEBVTT

00:18:59.084 --> 00:19:00.912
how are you going about learning now?"

00:19:00.936 --> 00:19:02.456
And I think it was those words.

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.226
And I went, "Oh." (Laughs)

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:07.395
I was just completely bouncing
from thing to thing

00:19:07.419 --> 00:19:08.935
without actually having a plan,

00:19:08.959 --> 00:19:11.237
and I'd not even sat down and gone,

00:19:11.261 --> 00:19:13.861
"Right, Rachel, what do you actually
need to learn here

00:19:13.885 --> 00:19:16.218
to become comfortable with the role?"

00:19:16.242 --> 00:19:18.528
AG: Victoria helped Rachel
plan actionable steps

00:19:18.552 --> 00:19:20.699
to build up her tech knowledge at work.

00:19:20.723 --> 00:19:23.184
She started reading books
on cloud technology.

00:19:23.208 --> 00:19:25.702
She reached out to some
coworkers to get up to speed.

00:19:25.726 --> 00:19:28.947
She even signed up for a coding class,
run by a colleague.

00:19:28.971 --> 00:19:30.694
RB: So I went along to one of these